# Debugging workflow for this app

When debugging UI behavior, layout regressions, or interaction bugs:

1. Reproduce in browser automation first (local app URL), not code-only guessing.
2. Capture runtime evidence before changing code:
   - element bounds (`getBoundingClientRect`)
   - computed styles (`position`, `top/bottom/left/right`, `display`, sizing)
   - viewport/document metrics and scroll offsets
3. Form 3-5 concrete hypotheses, then instrument minimal logs to prove/disprove each.
4. Fix only after evidence identifies root cause.
5. Keep instrumentation through at least one post-fix verification run.
6. Remove instrumentation only after verification succeeds and user confirms.

For modal/overlay issues, validate the overlay itself is truly viewport-anchored and not constrained by parent layout.
